==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Lost World Yuki & Cat''' at level 10.

Evolves into '''Lost World Catgirl Yuki''' at level 30 using [[Catfruit]] and XP.

==Strategy/Usage==
Lost World Yuki is a nuker with massive damage against Alien and Angel enemies. Yuki is very comparable to [[Thundia (Uber Rare Cat)|Thundia]] or [[Windy (Uber Rare Cat)|Windy]] with similar range, DPS and knockback count. Her usage against both traits are very similar. While she can be used well as a nuker, there is little special about her. She has better usage against Angels simply because of fewer Angel backliners existing. She can be useful against enemies like [[Winged Pigge]], [[Chickful A]], [[I.M. Phace]] and [[Scissoroo]].

==='''True Form'''===
Lost World Yuki & Cat gains a roughly 20% boost in attack power (3.6k DPS to 4.3k DPS at level 30) and a 25% increase in health (34k to 42.5k at level 30), improving her general usage. Other additions are 100% barrier breaker, which is always a plus, and knockback immune. While she still isn't a great generalist, she is now better in mixed stages with the True Form overall improving her usability.

==='''Talents'''===
The Target Aku talent allows Lost World Catgirl Yuki to target another trait to have massive damage against. However, hard-pushing Aku are not a great match against Yuki, requiring further upgrading for her to be used effectively. In addition, there are better options for [[:Category:Anti-Aku Cats|Anti-Aku]] units. For these reasons along with the high cost, the Target Aku and Resist Surge talents are not recommended.

==='''Orb'''===
The only worthwhile orbs that Lost World Yuki can equip are either Massive Damage Orb against Angel/Alien/Aku or a Strengthen Orb, all of which improve her damage significantly.

